# Declared deviations of ooxargs.
#
# A case line written here is a deviation the owner declares: the exit
# code still has to be the same as the upstream tool, but the text of the
# answer may differ. Every other case has to match the upstream tool
# byte for byte.
#
# Write the case line as it stands in qa/parity/cases.oot, with its
# match word in front of it.
#
# A deviation is not a way to make the gate pass. The exit code of a
# declared case is still compared with the exit code of the upstream
# tool, and a case whose exit code differs is a failure that has to be
# fixed in the tool. A deviation says that the tool answers the same
# question the same way and words the answer its own way.
#
# The cases come from the test recipe of the repository, so a case line
# that is not in the table is a line the recipe does not hold any more.
# Such a line is ignored, and it does not change the gate.
